WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
And I want this to be very clear in how this works.

00:00:07.040 --> 00:00:10.140
It's not the LLM itself running the function.

00:00:10.140 --> 00:00:13.340
Instead, what the LLM is doing is taking

00:00:13.340 --> 00:00:16.780
the function description, the name of the function, and the inputs of the function,

00:00:16.780 --> 00:00:20.040
a description of what the function does, and an expected output.

00:00:20.040 --> 00:00:22.580
And it's taking that and passing it to the runtime,

00:00:22.580 --> 00:00:25.380
which in our case—later—we'll look at Python.

00:00:25.380 --> 00:00:27.780
It's taking that and passing it to the runtime.
